<Base title="About">
  <div class="about">
    <h1>About Problem Atlas</h1>
    <p>Problem Atlas collects the evidence on India's biggest problems in one place, and puts the solutions being tried right next to them, so readers can move from "what is wrong" to "what works".</p>
    <h2>How sources are chosen</h2>
    <p>We prefer government statistics, peer-reviewed research, reports from established institutions, and reporting from reputable outlets. Every figure on a problem page names its source.</p>
    <h2>Going global</h2>
    <p>Every entry is tagged with a region. India comes first; other countries will be added region by region, and the same problems can then be compared across countries.</p>
    <h2>Suggest a resource</h2>
    <p>A contribution form is planned. It will let anyone suggest an article, paper or video for review.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
